  "question": {
    "text": "A sub-atomic particle of mass $10^{-30} \\mathrm{~kg}$ is moving with a velocity $2.21 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$. Under the matter wave consideration, the particle will behave closely like $\\qquad$ $\\left(\\mathrm{h}=6.63 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{~J} . \\mathrm{s}\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "LvmUV",
      "text": "Visible radiation",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "grwnE",
      "text": "Gamma rays",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "af4JX",
      "text": "Infra-red radiation",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4zhB2",
      "text": "X-rays",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\lambda=\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{\\mathrm{p}}=\\frac{6.63 \\times 10^{-34}}{10^{-30} \\times 2.21 \\times 10^6} \\\\\n& =3 \\times 10^{-10} \\mathrm{~m}\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nHence particle will behave as x-ray.",
    "image": null
  },
